<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-8025] Result of GridTestUtils.runMultiThreadedAsync has a bug in cancel() implementation</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-8025</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;GridTestUtils.runMultiThreadedAsync returns a future with cancel() support, but cancellation implementation never interrupts threads that execute user-provided tasks. That is, those threads can continue their execution even after test method finishes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The reproducer attached demonstrates activity from threads created by test0 after test0 finished and test1 is being run.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="13147199">IGNITE-8025</key>
